::GEO_U04_L04_Q01::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U04_L04_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.SIM.1<br><br>Question:<br>Two similar figures have corresponding sides 5 and 20. What is the scale factor from first to second? {
=A. 4#20 divided by 5 equals 4.
~B. 15#This subtracts instead of comparing by ratio.
~C. 25#This adds the side lengths.
~D. &frac14;#This is the reverse scale factor. T
}

